@@ -0,0 +1,166 @@
+# PayPal integration plan & contract sheet
+
+## Scope
+Add PayPal/Venmo/Pay Later (web SDK v6) beside card checkout. Fulfil only after a server capture (or verified `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` webhook) whose COMPLETED capture amount/currency and `custom_id` match a server-priced shop order. Keep card checkout and `npm test` green.
+
+## Repo survey (pattern + exemplar)
+- ESM (`"type":"module"`), Express 5, Node >=22, `node:test`. Exemplar server: `server.js` (`createApp({db,cards,adminKey})`, `express.json`, routes return `{error}` JSON).
+- Pricing validation exemplar: `lib/cart.js` `priceCart(items)` — SKUs/qty only, integer cents, currency `"usd"`, qty integer 1..10 (`MAX_QTY_PER_LINE=10`), unknown SKU throws. Reuse it unchanged for PayPal (hardening #1,#11).
+- DB exemplar: `lib/db.js` `openDb` (`node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync`, prepared statements). Fulfilment exemplar: `lib/fulfilment.js` `fulfilOrder(db,id)` prints a label every call — call it only on an atomic paid-claim.
+- Frontend exemplar: `public/app.js` (bag in localStorage, sends only `{sku,qty}`), `public/index.html` `#payment-options` holds card form, `public/styles.css`.
+- Baseline before edits: `npm test` = 5 pass. Package manager npm. No tsconfig in shop (JS ESM); type-check gate = `node --check` on touched files + SDK-shape fidelity from this sheet (no `tsc` project to run; stated in final report).
+- Toolchain: Node v24.22.2, npm 11.19.1.
+
+## SDK identity (from `typescript-getting-started` + installed map)
+- Package `paypal` v2.29.0, import specifier `paypal` (root only, no deep imports), client `PaypalClient`, `new PaypalClient(options: ClientOptions={})`.
+- Installed pinned over https: `git+https://github.com/context-plugins/paypal-typescript-sdk#5d0df8a8817e5fdf2e2cd48e68f790ea4730aab2` (commit of `main` at install; `node -e "console.log(require.resolve('paypal/package.json'))"` resolves, `node_modules/paypal/sdk-map.md` present). Node floor >=20.3 — shop Node 24 OK.
+- This SDK's `ClientOptions` (src/client-options.ts/src/servers.ts): `serverOptions?: { baseUrl?: string }` — flat baseUrl override (NOT nested group/env; this SDK declares one environment, no `ServerEnvironment`). Default base `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`. Fields: `serverOptions, retry, logging, fetch, oauth2, oauth2Strategy`.
+- Auth: `oauth2: {clientId, clientSecret}` OAuth2 client-credentials; token `POST {base}/v1/oauth2/token` via same client/fetch/baseUrl, cached on the long-lived client, Basic header. Unset credential = no failure at construction, 401 later — so factory must throw if id/secret missing when PayPal is configured.
+- SDK is ESM+CJS dual; shop is pure ESM (`import` only) so `instanceof` on SDK errors is reliable in-process. Do NOT import model type `Error` unaliased (shadows global); in JS we import only runtime values `PaypalClient, PaypalError` and refer to wire/model shapes from this sheet.
+- Logging: set `logging:{level:"off"}` explicitly (blocks `PAYPAL_CLIENT_LOG` arming it), never `logRequestBody`, no per-call `logging` level. No hooks/middleware — `ClientOptions.fetch` is the only transport seam, forward the `Request`/its signal.
+- Retry: SDK retries on by default (GET etc). Use `retry:{maxRetries:0, timeout:10000}` on the one client — our code owns write recovery (re-read), never stack retries on writes.
+- Build client ONCE in a factory (`createPayPalService`), hold for process life (token cache + memoized `client.orders`).
+
+## Host / environment decision
+- Every PayPal REST call base = `PAYPAL_API_BASE` env (default `https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com`), passed as `serverOptions:{baseUrl: PAYPAL_API_BASE}`. Token follows same base automatically.
+- `PAYPAL_ENV` is `sandbox|live` and selects ONLY the browser script: sandbox `https://www.sandbox.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`, live `https://www.paypal.com/web-sdk/v6/core`. Never infer env from `PAYPAL_API_BASE` (harness proxy). Unknown `PAYPAL_ENV` => treat as sandbox script? No: default `sandbox` when unset, reject other values at service construction.
+- Browser `testBuyerCountry`: only sandbox + `PAYPAL_TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY` set; unset => key omitted entirely.
+
+## Operations in scope (one pass, from map/operations/orders.md)
+All: flat channel-blind request, `op(request, options?)`, `ApiPromise<T,E>`, auth `oauth2`, server group default. SDK sends `Idempotency-Key` minted per call on non-GET plus identity headers — not ours, no row needed for them; caller idempotency uses declared `PayPal-Request-Id` field where listed.
+
+### createOrder — `client.orders.createOrder(request: Orders.CreateOrderRequest): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CreateOrderError>`
+Wire `POST /v2/checkout/orders`. Fields: `payPalMockResponse` header `PayPal-Mock-Response` opt; `payPalRequestId` header `PayPal-Request-Id` opt; `payPalPartnerAttributionId` header opt; `payPalClientMetadataId` header opt; `prefer` header `Prefer` opt default `"return=minimal"`; `payPalAuthAssertion` header opt; `body: OrderRequest` body REQUIRED.
+Error arms (tag=status): `error`=400, `error2`=401, `error3`=422, `error4`=default, `undeclared`=raw. Body model `Error` {name:string req, message:string req, debugId (`debug_id`):string req, details?: ErrorDetails[{issue:string req, field?,value?,location? default body,description?}], links?}.
+`OrderRequest` (src/models/order-request.ts): `intent: CheckoutPaymentIntent` req (`Capture:"CAPTURE"`, `Authorize:"AUTHORIZE"`), `purchaseUnits: PurchaseUnitRequest[]` req, `processingInstruction?`, `payer?`, `paymentSource?`, `applicationContext?` (wire purchase_units etc).
+`PurchaseUnitRequest`: `amount: AmountWithBreakdown` req, `referenceId?`, `payee?`, `paymentInstruction?`, `description?`, `customId?` (wire custom_id), `invoiceId?` (invoice_id), `softDescriptor?`, `items?: ItemRequest[]`, `shipping?`, `supplementaryData?`.
+`AmountWithBreakdown`: `currencyCode` req (currency_code), `value` req string, `breakdown?: {itemTotal?: Money, shipping?, handling?, taxTotal?, insurance?, shippingDiscount?, discount?}` (item_total...). `Money`: `currencyCode` req, `value` req string.
+`ItemRequest`: `name` req, `unitAmount: Money` req (unit_amount), `quantity` req string, `tax?`, `description?`, `sku?`, `url?`, `category?`, `imageUrl?`, `upc?`, `billingPlan?`.
+Returns `Order` (all optional — assert `id !== undefined` after call): `id?`, `status?: OrderStatus` (CREATED/SAVED/APPROVED/VOIDED/COMPLETED/PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED), `purchaseUnits?: PurchaseUnit[]`, `intent?`, links etc. `PurchaseUnit`: `amount?: AmountWithBreakdown`, `customId?`, `invoiceId?`, `referenceId?`, `payments?: {captures?: OrdersCapture[], authorizations?, refunds?}`, `items?`. `OrdersCapture`: `status?: CaptureStatus` (COMPLETED/DECLINED/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED/PENDING/REFUNDED/FAILED), `id?`, `amount?: Money`, `invoiceId?`, `customId?`, `finalCapture` default false, `disbursementMode` default INSTANT.
+
+### captureOrder — `client.orders.captureOrder(request: Orders.CaptureOrderRequest): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.CaptureOrderError>`
+Wire `POST /v2/checkout/orders/{id}/capture`. Fields: `id` path req string; `payPalMockResponse` header opt; `payPalRequestId` header `PayPal-Request-Id` opt; `prefer` header opt default `"return=minimal"`; `payPalClientMetadataId`, `payPalAuthAssertion` opt; `body?: OrderCaptureRequest` opt (`{paymentSource?}` only). **Contract corrected by real sandbox (2026-11-08): despite being optional in the SDK, `body` MUST be passed as `{}` — omitting it sends no body and no `Content-Type`, and real PayPal answered `415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE: The request payload is not supported` (debug `ca571d11c6846`) leaving the order pending. Passing `body: {}` makes the SDK send `"{}"` with `Content-Type: application/json`.**
+Error arms: `error`=400, `error2`=401, `error3`=403, `error4`=404, `error5`=422, `error6`=500, `error7`=default, `undeclared`. Same `Error` body model.
+
+### getOrder — `client.orders.getOrder(request: Orders.GetOrderRequest): ApiPromise<Order, Orders.GetOrderError>`
+Wire `GET /v2/checkout/orders/{id}`. Fields: `id` path req, `fields` query opt, `payPalMockResponse`, `payPalAuthAssertion` headers opt. Error arms: `error`=401, `error2`=404, `error3`=default, `undeclared`. Returns `Order` — assert `id`, `purchaseUnits` members we depend on.
+
+No SDK operation exists for webhook verification (40 ops: orders/payments/vault/transactionSearch/subscriptions only) — `POST /v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature` and its client-credentials token are therefore direct `fetch` calls to `PAYPAL_API_BASE` in our service (same injectable `fetch` seam, same base). This is the one PayPal REST surface the SDK does not cover; recorded here, not filled from memory: body `{auth_algo,cert_url,transmission_id,transmission_sig,transmission_time,webhook_id,webhook_event}` per hardening #6 task contract.
+
+## Response-mode & member assertions
+Await (throwing) mode everywhere (no success headers needed). After each success assert depended members: create `order.id`; capture/get `id`, `purchaseUnits[0].customId`, captures' `status/amount`. A missing member = provider-unreadable/unknown, never paid. `DecodeError` (kind decode) on a 2xx is unknown for writes, not failure.
+
+## Amount conversion (hardening #2)
+One function `centsToPayPalAmount(cents)` in `lib/paypal.js` (integer math): 4900->"49.00", 5->"0.05", 300->"3.00". Currency: shop `usd` -> PayPal `"USD"`. Items: unitAmount per catalog unit cents, quantity `String(qty)`, breakdown `item_total` == total value, amount.value == total. Parse webhook dollars->cents with string split (no floats).
+
+## 1b.1 DURABLE WRITES
+Claim order for every write: claim row -> SDK call -> record result.
+
+DUPLICATE CLAIMS
+| Write | Where the claim is stored | What rejects the second one | Where that rejection is caught | Where in the code |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| createOrder | `payment_claims` row, claim_key=`create:<shopOrderId>` (shop order created first in `orders`) + orders.paypal_order_id UNIQUE | PRIMARY KEY on payment_claims.claim_key (shopOrderId derived once per shop order) and UNIQUE(orders.paypal_order_id); driver error recognised by /UNIQUE constraint failed/ message check via code-or-message helper `isUniqueViolation` | try/catch around `db.tryClaim(...)` in create route; loser uses winner's stored paypal_order_id | `lib/db.js:tryClaim/isUniqueViolation`, `server.js POST /api/paypal/orders` (claim before `paypalService.createOrder`); claim-present asserted inside faked fetch in `test/paypal.test.js` create test |
+| captureOrder | `payment_claims` row, claim_key=`capture:<shopOrderId>` inserted BEFORE SDK call | PRIMARY KEY on claim_key (same shop order for every caller) | try/catch around `db.tryClaim(...)` in capture path; loser settles by re-reading PayPal order (getOrder), never captures twice blindly | `lib/db.js:tryClaim`, `server.js POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` (claim before `paypalService.captureOrder`, second caller -> `settleViaGetOrder`); tested by concurrent-capture test |
+
+`PayPal-Request-Id` sent on create/capture = shopOrderId (the claim's stored reference), so provider-side joins our retries. SDK's own per-call Idempotency-Key sits beside, never replaces, this.
+Release claim when provider refuses (ApiError 4xx incl INSTRUMENT_DECLINED, AuthError, EncodeError): delete claim row so a later legitimate attempt is not blocked. On success/PENDING keep shop order pending/paid flow; capture claim is released after the outcome is settled (paid/pending/refused/unknown-settled) — the atomic paid transition, not the claim, is the fulfil-once guard thereafter; an already-paid order short-circuits before any new claim.
+
+UNKNOWN OUTCOMES
+| Write | The operation you re-read with | The reference you search by | Where in the code | The test that fails the connection |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| createOrder | getOrder | payPalRequestId=shopOrderId cannot be searched by id before we know PayPal id — NO search-by-request-id op exists in SDK. Blocker mitigated: on connection/timeout after create, outcome unknown: return 502 unknown, leave shop order pending with claim released, create a NEW shop order on buyer retry (PayPal-Request-Id per shop order makes a same-order retry joinable only if route is retried for same shop order; our create route makes a fresh shop order per request, so an unknown create is abandoned unpaid/unfulfilled — safe, never paid) | `server.js POST /api/paypal/orders` catch -> 502 unknown, claim released | N/A for create (no re-read possible, documented blocker); capture connection tests prove re-read path |
+| captureOrder | getOrder | PayPal order id (path id we captured) | `server.js settleViaGetOrder` called from capture catch on unknown/ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED | `test/paypal.test.js`: 'connection failure on capture re-reads...' (asserts GET was made) and 'ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED settles by re-reading'; never-sent (401/auth path) uses no re-read — covered by 401 test expecting direct 502 |
+
+Never-sent failures (AuthError kind auth, EncodeError kind encode) get NO re-read and a 502 config/integration outcome. Connection/timeout/decode-on-write: re-read; found COMPLETED-matching => settle paid; not found / re-read fails => 502 "outcome unknown", never "failed", never markFailed.
+
+## 1b.2 CROSS-OPERATION INVARIANTS
+| Invariant | Where the legal set comes from | Enforced where | The test that proves it |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Capture/get/webhook settle only the shop order bound at create: purchase-unit `custom_id` == shop order id, and PayPal order id == orders.paypal_order_id stored at create | Our `orders` row (created before createOrder) | settle function before any paid claim; capture route first loads shop order BY PayPal order id | fake capture with wrong custom_id/foreign paypal id => unpaid, capture/settle rejected |
+| Capture amount+currency == shop order total (USD) | Shop order total_cents from catalog pricing | settle function | fake COMPLETED capture with 0.01 => unpaid, no shipment |
+| SKUs/qty legal | `lib/catalog.js` via priceCart | create route before shop order + claim | existing priceCart tests + replay test with price fields ignored |
+
+## 1b.3 OPTIONAL REQUEST FIELDS
+createOrder request:
+| Field | What requires it | Set it? |
+|---|---|---|
+| payPalRequestId | DUPLICATE CLAIMS row (shopOrderId) | ✅ = shopOrderId |
+| prefer | we depend on full representation (id/purchase_units/captures on response) — SDK default return=minimal may omit them | ✅ `"return=representation"` |
+| payPalMockResponse | nothing (attacker-controllable negative testing) | ❌ leave out, never forward browser headers |
+| payPalPartnerAttributionId / payPalClientMetadataId / payPalAuthAssertion | nothing | ❌ |
+| body.intent | required member; task capture-immediately | ✅ CheckoutPaymentIntent.Capture = "CAPTURE" |
+| body.purchaseUnits[0].customId / invoiceId | hardening #3 bind PayPal order to shop order | ✅ shopOrderId |
+| body.purchaseUnits[0].amount.breakdown.itemTotal | hardening #2 breakdown sums to total | ✅ |
+| body.purchaseUnits[0].items[] (name,unitAmount,quantity,sku) | hardening #2 item breakdown | ✅ |
+| all other OrderRequest/PurchaseUnitRequest/ItemRequest optionals (payer, paymentSource, applicationContext, payee, description, shipping, tax, category...) | nothing | ❌ |
+
+captureOrder request:
+| Field | What requires it | Set it? |
+|---|---|---|
+| payPalRequestId | DUPLICATE CLAIMS row | ✅ = shopOrderId |
+| prefer | need captures[] in response to verify COMPLETED/amount | ✅ `"return=representation"` |
+| payPalMockResponse / payPalClientMetadataId / payPalAuthAssertion | nothing | ❌ never forward |
+| body | real sandbox requires a JSON payload: omitting it sends no `Content-Type` and PayPal returns 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE (debug ca571d11c6846) | ✅ `body: {}` (empty JSON object, no `paymentSource`) |
+
+getOrder request: `fields`, `payPalMockResponse`, `payPalAuthAssertion` — nothing requires => ❌ all omitted, only `id`.
+Test proving it: faked-fetch test parses every SDK-built request and asserts no header/body key beyond sheet rows (allow SDK-sent: authorization, content-type, idempotency-key, identity headers).
+
+## 1b.4 WHEN THE API SAYS NO (per operation, caller = browser checkout)
+Reason extraction: for typed arms read `err.payload.body` (Error model: message + details[].issue/description) when payload.kind != "undeclared"; for undeclared decode rawBody text, try JSON message/name — never put SDK `err.message` (method+URL) on the wire. Log reason + status server-side AND return it per table.
+
+createOrder / getOrder / captureOrder (same ladder, capture extras below):
+| status | your app answers | the caller reads | test |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 4xx other than 401/403/429 | same 4xx | API reason text from err.payload | fake 422/400 with reason; assert reason in response, order unpaid |
+| 401/403 | 502 | fixed "Payment provider unavailable." (our credentials) | fake 401; assert 502 + fixed text, reason NOT leaked beyond PayPal's own 4xx rule — 401/403 fixed only |
+| 429 | 503 | fixed temporarily-unavailable | — (ladder code shared, covered by unit mapping test if cheap) |
+| 5xx | 502 | fixed provider-error | fake 500 on capture => 502, unpaid |
+| no response, on a write | per UNKNOWN OUTCOMES (re-read capture; create = unknown 502) | "outcome unknown", never failed | connection-fail tests below |
+| no response, on a read | 502 | fixed | getOrder connection fail in capture-settle => unknown 502 |
+
+capture extras: 422 details issue `INSTRUMENT_DECLINED` => 422, body `{error:<PayPal reason>, code:"INSTRUMENT_DECLINED"}`, order stays **pending** (buyer picks another method, can re-click; v6 skill §4). `TRANSACTION_REFUSED`/other 422 issues => 422 with PayPal reason, pending/unpaid. `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` => re-read getOrder and settle from PayPal (hardening #10), not an error to buyer if capture COMPLETED-matching (return paid). Capture status `PENDING` => 202 `{status:"pending"}`, no fulfil; `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` webhook settles later. Capture `DECLINED`/`FAILED` status in a 2xx => 422 unpaid.
+
+Webhook verify failures: verification_status != SUCCESS => 400, change nothing (event NOT recorded). Missing transmission headers => 400. Token/verify transport failure => 502, change nothing.
+
+## Webhooks (hardening #6,#7,#9)
+`POST /api/paypal/webhooks`. Verify BEFORE trusting: token via `POST {PAYPAL_API_BASE}/v1/oauth2/token` (Basic, client_credentials), then verify call with headers' auth_algo/cert_url/transmission_id/transmission_sig/transmission_time + `webhook_id: PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` + parsed `webhook_event`. Only `SUCCESS` proceeds.
+Idempotency: `webhook_events(event_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY)` inserted after verification, before acting; duplicate insert => 200, no change.
+Act: `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` => locate shop order (resource.custom_id = shop id, else supplementary_data.related_ids.order_id -> orders.paypal_order_id), require resource.status COMPLETED (event implies), amount string parsed to cents == total_cents and currency == USD (case-insens), custom_id matches; then atomic claim. `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` and all other types: record + 200, never paid. Out-of-order/duplicate after paid: atomic claim changes 0 rows, no fulfil, no backwards.
+
+## Fulfil exactly once (hardening #8,#4)
+`db.claimPaidForPayPal(id,...)`: `UPDATE orders SET status='paid', payment_method='paypal', payment_reference=?, paid_cents=?, paid_at=? WHERE id=? AND status='pending'`; fulfil only if `changes===1`, then `fulfilOrder` (sets fulfilled). Concurrent capture+webhook: loser changes 0, no second label. Note card flow keeps existing markPaid+fulfil (its test expects fulfilled).
+
+## DB changes (lib/db.js, additive, migration-safe)
+- orders: add `paypal_order_id TEXT UNIQUE` (CREATE for fresh; PRAGMA table_info check + ALTER for existing files).
+- `webhook_events(event_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, event_type TEXT, created_at TEXT)`, `payment_claims(claim_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, shop_order_id TEXT, paypal_order_id TEXT, created_at TEXT)`.
+- Methods: `setPaypalOrderId`, `getOrderByPaypalId`, `tryClaim(key,shop,paypal)`->bool, `releaseClaim(key)`, `claimPaidForPayPal`, `recordWebhookEvent(id,type)`->bool.
+
+## Routes (server.js, createApp gains optional `paypal` service; default built from env when creds present)
+- `GET /api/paypal/config` => `{clientId, scriptUrl, currency:"USD", ...(sandbox&&testBuyerCountry?{testBuyerCountry}:{})}` — client id only, never secret (hardening #12).
+- `POST /api/paypal/orders` `{items,email}` — ignores any price/amount/total/currency keys (priceCart only). Create shop order (method paypal) -> claim -> SDK create -> store paypal_order_id -> `{id:<paypalOrderId>, orderId:<shopId>}`. Browser maps `{orderId: data.id}`.
+- `POST /api/paypal/orders/:paypalOrderId/capture` — load shop order by paypal id (404 if none), if already paid/fulfilled return current status; claim -> SDK capture -> validate/settle -> `{orderId, status}`.
+- `POST /api/paypal/webhooks` as above.
+- Production main: build paypal service from env (PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID/SECRET/API_BASE/WEBHOOK_ID/ENV/TEST_BUYER_COUNTRY); if creds absent, paypal=null (config returns clientId null, paypal routes 503) so card shop still boots locally; injected service in tests.
+
+## Browser (heistproof:paypal-web-sdk-v6)
+- Fetch `/api/paypal/config`, dynamically load `scriptUrl` once (never hardcode env twice), `onload` init.
+- `sdk = await window.paypal.createInstance({clientId, components:["paypal-payments","venmo-payments","paypal-messages"], pageType:"checkout", ...(testBuyerCountry?{testBuyerCountry}:{})})`; `methods = await sdk.findEligibleMethods({currencyCode:"USD"})`; unhide only eligible of paypal/venmo/paylater; paylater details `methods.getDetails("paylater")` -> set button.productCode/countryCode before unhide.
+- Buttons `<paypal-button type="pay">`, `<venmo-button>`, `<paypal-pay-later-button>` hidden in index.html beside card form.
+- One session per method (`createPayPalOneTimePaymentSession`/`createVenmoOneTimePaymentSession`/`createPayLaterOneTimePaymentSession`) with shared onApprove (POST capture route; server decides paid; 422 INSTRUMENT_DECLINED => show "choose another way to pay"), onCancel, onError (show msg, never paid).
+- Click: `const p = createOrder(); await session.start({presentationMode:"auto"}, p);` — do NOT await createOrder first (popup activation). createOrder POSTs bag `{sku,qty}` only, returns `{orderId: data.id}`.
+- Pay Later message: `<paypal-message amount currency-code="USD" auto-bootstrap>` after `sdk.createPayPalMessages()`, update `amount` (decimal string from bag total cents) on `bag:change`.
+
+## Assumptions & Blockers
+- Minor: SDK has no webhook-verify operation (map checked) — direct fetch to PAYPAL_API_BASE for token+verify, documented above. No live calls during build (no creds); harness runs sandbox after.
+- Minor: unknown outcome on createOrder cannot be re-read by request-id (no such SDK op) — abandoned pending shop order, buyer retry creates a new one; never paid/fulfilled, so safe.
+- No blockers requiring user answer.
+
+## REQUIRED READING
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-error-handling` (loaded — error ladder, arm tags per operation, rethrow outside family)
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-client-initialization` (loaded — build once, serverOptions.baseUrl override, logging off explicit)
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-authentication` (loaded — oauth2 creds, AuthError = never sent, validate at factory)
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-calling-endpoints` (loaded — flat request, prefer default sent, ApiPromise)
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-models` (loaded — required vs optional, Money strings end-to-end, Error alias warning)
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-configuration-resilience` (loaded — retry off for writes, fetch seam forwards Request/signal, no stacked retries)
+- MUST load `paypal:typescript-testing` (loaded — fake fetch via ClientOptions.fetch, token request first, retry maxRetries 0, wire-shaped stubs)
+All loaded before implementation, per Step 1c floor.
